WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.702
Here's the build mapped onto the Federal

2
00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.675
Modernization Workbook's
Book 07's six waves.

3
00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:10.245
This is the platform work that runs
alongside the Cloud PKI waves,

4
00:00:10.245 --> 00:00:11.938
with a gate added to each.

5
00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:13.900
It's program design guidance.

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.875
Wave 1, Assess, weeks one to four.

7
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:22.025
Stand up a two-server test cluster and
its SQL database inside the boundary.

8
00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:27.363
Run read-only network discovery and
import the AD CS templates in scope.

9
00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:30.693
That import needs the
privileged CA account,

10
00:00:30.693 --> 00:00:33.663
so create it now, under the ESC7 controls.

11
00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:38.968
Gate: every certificate without an
issuance record is logged as a finding,

12
00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.925
and the CA account is
in the ESC7 baseline.

13
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:43.663
Wave 2, Foundation.

14
00:00:43.663 --> 00:00:47.306
Build production: at least
two servers per role,

15
00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:50.388
a load balancer, Always
On, keys backed up.

16
00:00:50.388 --> 00:00:55.038
Decide FIPS mode per server,
with ACME on its own servers.

17
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:58.003
Replace the operational certificates,

18
00:00:58.003 --> 00:01:03.034
set up Entra single sign-on and syslog
over TLS, build the policy tree,

19
00:01:03.034 --> 00:01:06.717
one CA template object per
AD CS template, a CA pool,

20
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:10.850
the public CA driver and the
password-vault connection.

21
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:16.462
Gate: a rehearsed restore, a passing
negative test, and IIS hardening applied.

22
00:01:16.462 --> 00:01:18.050
Wave 3, Pilot.

23
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:24.237
Move pilot servers onto platform renewal,
IIS, Apache, F5, NetScaler and one NPS

24
00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:27.717
server, assign Server
Owners, and pilot ACME,

25
00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:31.100
with autoenrollment left on for rollback.

26
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.925
Wave 4, Scale, moves servers
ring by ring off autoenrollment.

27
00:01:35.925 --> 00:01:39.363
Wave 5 puts all public
TLS on the platform.

28
00:01:39.363 --> 00:01:42.912
Wave 6 retires CAs on
the inventory's evidence.

29
00:01:42.912 --> 00:01:48.373
Sources: Research brief section 9
(program design guidance); Book 07,

30
00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:53.039
Chapter 07 (migration playbook,
waves 1 to 6 and exit gates),

31
00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:58.202
Chapter 04 (issuer decision for
internal server certificates),

32
00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:02.230
Chapter 08 (drift patterns
and decommissioning).
